<p>In this release we made it possible to set an ablation value on ammo. When a target is shot with a particular ammo, the system
will look up that value and subtract it from the SP on the target's armor. For armor-piercing rounds this value is 2, for rubber
rounds it is 0, and for almost everything else it is 1. This allows us to better support some DLC items too, such as the 
Malorian Arms Sub-Flechette ammo that has an ablation value of 4.</p>

<p>You should have seen a quick data migration that took care of homebrew ammo items for you, if your world had any. Justo to be
sure, you may want to check them to be confident the ablation is still what you expect.</p>